From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:45:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/44] qwen27: carry the mHC window's residual in its own
 stream planes

The reference keeps a window's residual as the flattened streams between
boundaries, and its hidden states show it: after the first mHC layer they are
8192 wide, and the two halves genuinely differ. The engine's norm and every
projection row-stride by , so the window gets its own buffer and the
boundary kernels read and write it stream-major.

With this the looped checkpoint runs 56 executions with per-visit caches and
reproduces the first token on all three prompts, and two prompts agree for 22
and 33 of 64 greedy tokens against the reference run on the same 4-bit values. A
seam-level mismatch remains inside the window and is recorded in STATUS.md.
---
 zig/kernels/metal/qwen27/mhc.metal  | 19 ++++++-------
 zig/src/families/qwen27/forward.zig | 41 ++++++++++++++---------------
 zig/src/families/qwen27/mhc.zig     | 18 ++++++-------
 zig/tests/qwen27/mhc_check.zig      |  9 +++----
 4 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 45 deletions(-)

